(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #108: the constant-length shape, `Set t to "n={n}"` -
 each evaluation is a fresh, similarly-sized buffer, so the leak here is
 linear rather than quadratic, but still unbounded. Measured before the
 fix: maxrss 160 MB at 40000 iterations. Same measurement technique as
 564 - see that test's header comment.)

a text called t is "".
a number called n is 0.
While n is less than 40000, Set t to "n={n}", increment n.

a buffer called statm is 256 bytes in size.
open a file for reading called procfile at "/proc/self/statm".
Read from procfile into statm.
Close procfile.

a number called i is 1.
While i is less than or equal to statm's size and byte i of statm is not 32, increment i.
increment i.

a number called resident is 0.
a number called digit is 0.
While i is less than or equal to statm's size and byte i of statm is not 32 and byte i of statm is not 10,
    Set digit to byte i of statm,
    Set resident to resident multiply 10 add digit subtract 48,
    increment i.

If resident is less than 5000
    Print "ok".
Otherwise
    Print resident.
